                "photoUrl": "https://static.swapcard.com/public/images/02b261c04d354fd79eb59ec48642de8c.jpeg",
                "organization": "Invest India",
                "biography": "Dr. Suruchi Mittar is a seasoned leader with over 25 years of experience in academia, corporate governance, and policy advocacy. As Chief Industry Officer at Invest India, she drives investment in key sectors like tourism, media, and pharmaceuticals. With her Ph.D. in Philosophy, Dr. Mittar brings unique insights to her leadership. She has led initiatives to promote innovation, sustainability, and inclusive growth in India and globally.\n\nPrior to her current role, Dr. Mittar founded Sanai Changemakers, where she focused on strategic HR, leadership development, and organizational design. She has also served as a senior faculty member at the prestigious National Institute of Fashion Technology for more than 15 years.\n\nDr. Mittar has leveraged her expertise across diverse geographies, including the UK, Europe, Australia, Bangladesh, Jordan, and Ethiopia, to optimize operations and empower communities. Her leadership is characterized by a holistic approach, encompassing strategic vision, operational excellence, and a deep-seated commitment to ethical business practices.\n\nAt Invest India, Dr. Mittar has been instrumental in transforming the Tourism Team into a strategic hub that bridges the gap between government and private investment opportunities. She has developed a unified framework to align diverse stakeholders, fostering a favorable environment for increased investment in India's tourism sector.\n\nHer leadership extends to elevating India's art and craft sector, as well as developing strategic frameworks for promoting Indian industries in countries like Myanmar. Collaborating with global organizations such as the International Labour Organization (ILO) and the United Nations Environment Programme (UNEP), Dr. Mittar's work underscores her global vision, commitment to sustainable development, and passion for inclusive growth.",
