                "organization": "Dubai Chambers",
                "biography": "Maha Al Gargawi is the Vice President of Business Advocacy at Dubai Chambers. In this role, she drives proactive and reactive business and legislative advocacy recommendations and engagement with the government. \nPrior to joining Dubai Chambers, Maha was the Senior Vice President of Political Affairs at Expo 2020 Dubai and she also held the role of Vice President of International Participants at Expo 2020.\nPrior to Expo 2020, Maha was the Deputy General Counsel at Emirates Nuclear Energy Corporation.\nMaha also sits on the board of the German-Emirati Joint Council for Industry and Commerce. \nShe began her career working for Clifford Chance, a law firm based in London.\nShe holds a master’s and a bachelor’s degree in international commercial law from universities in the UK.",
