                "photoUrl": "https://static.swapcard.com/public/images/d9434718dced4231a1dfcc3eda2ea234.jpeg",
                "organization": "Four Seasons",
                "biography": "Graduating from the University of Michigan with a focus in Organizational Behavior, Amanda also completed further studies at University College London, holding a Nutrition Certification from the National Academy of Sports Management (NASM) and previously served as the President of the Hawaii Spa Association.\n\nFrom starting her career at a local spa business in Michigan, to leadership positions with renowned & international iconic hospitality brands including Elizabeth Arden, Starwood, WTS International and Marriott, Amanda has become a well-respected figure in the global spa & wellness industry.\n\nHaving previously played a pivotal role in launching the spa, pool & recreation areas of the St Regis, W Hotel & Westin complex at Habtoor City in Dubai, Amanda was also the Marriott Spa Regional Leader, marking her achievement of opening an illustrious 8 properties to date and supporting an additional 15 spas across the UAE.\n\nAmanda has been an integral part of the Four Seasons spa team for the past 6 years, not only as Senior Spa Director at Four Seasons Hualalai, but also overseeing spa operations at Four Seasons Oahu, Lanai, Bora Bora, St. Louis, and most notably, the opening of Four Seasons Cartagena, Columbia.",
